{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitBindingAmplitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitBindingAmplitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.q_sq_ne_one_of_qInt3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.q_sq_ne_one_of_qInt3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L186-L197","doc":"…and it is a PRIMITIVE one: `q² = 1` is incompatible with `[3]_q = 0`,\nsince there `q⁴ + q² + 1 = 3`.  (Needs `3 ≠ 0` in `K`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.q_pow_six_eq_one_of_qInt3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.q_pow_six_eq_one_of_qInt3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L179-L184","doc":"**The vanishing locus is a sixth root of unity.**  `q⁶ - 1 = (q² - 1)(q⁴ + q² + 1)`,\nso `[3]_q = 0` forces `q⁶ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_zero_iff_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_zero_iff_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L162-L177","doc":"`[3]_q = 0` is the cyclotomic condition `q⁴ + q² + 1 = 0`.\n(`qInt3 q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`, so multiply through by `q²`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hoefsmit_b_sq_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hoefsmit_b_sq_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L156-L160","doc":"**The amplitude vanishes exactly when `[3]_q` does** (given `[2]_q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.de_entanglement_fraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.de_entanglement_fraction","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L124-L128","doc":"The de-entanglement fraction: 1 - b² = 1/[2]_q². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hoefsmit_b_sq_eq_q3_over_q2sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hoefsmit_b_sq_eq_q3_over_q2sq","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L117-L122","doc":"The Hoefsmit binding amplitude identity:\nb² = [3]_q / [2]_q² = 1 - 1/[2]_q². ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hoefsmit-binding-amplitude","label":"prop:hoefsmit-binding-amplitude","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binding_amplitude_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binding_amplitude_iff","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L89-L105","doc":"**The Hoefsmit binding amplitude relation, division-free.**\n\nThe amplitude `b` is defined by `b² = [3]_q / [2]_q²`; written\nmultiplicatively that is `b² · [2]_q² = [3]_q`, which needs no\ndivision and no radical. This theorem says it is *equivalent* to the\nde-entanglement form `(1 − b²) · [2]_q² = 1` — i.e. `1 − b² = 1/[2]_q²`\n— over any commutative ring, with no non-vanishing hypotheses.\n\nThis is the central structural identity connecting the meson binding\ntopology to the q-integer tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_qInt2_sq_minus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_qInt2_sq_minus_one","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L81-L87","doc":"Key identity: [3]_q = [2]_q² - 1.\nProof: q² + 1 + q⁻² = (q+q⁻¹)² - 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2_sq_eq_h_sq_plus_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2_sq_eq_h_sq_plus_4","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L73-L79","doc":"Key identity: [2]_q² = h² + 4.\nProof: (q+q⁻¹)² = q² + 2 + q⁻² = (q-q⁻¹)² + 4 = h² + 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L61-L71","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket** for the `[3]_q` shorthand.\n\nOver a field the field-valued form needed `q ≠ 0` on top of `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`: the\nmiddle term of `q² + 1 + q⁻²` is `1 = q·q⁻¹`, which is `0` rather than `1` at\n`q = 0` under Lean's `0⁻¹ = 0`.  Carrying `q` as a **unit** discharges that\nhypothesis at the type level, so only the denominator guard survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L51-L59","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket** for the `[2]_q` shorthand.\n\nThe canonical `qIntBal` is a guarded division and stays over a field; this is\nwhere the unit-valued shorthand above meets it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt3","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L48-L49","doc":"The quantum integer [3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L45-L46","doc":"The quantum integer [2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_h","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hoefsmit-binding-amplitude.lean#L42-L43","doc":"The Hecke deformation parameter h = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}